{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790591380,"nonce":"9/Ov4jxfwL2E6Ui7o6PKVzc93K4=","title":"AOT: an #export thunk enters the runtime even for a body that cannot need it","message":"Requested by caribou: a Haxe call of a Wren #export costs far more than a Haxe call of Haxe on wasm, all of it in the thunk. Around an inlined body it raises the stack top, enters the program's context, snapshots the JIT roots, polls for an error, restores the roots and exits. Those calls also put the thunk and its callers in the fiber transform's suspend set. A member whose body is one block of instructions that cannot allocate, collect, suspend or raise once cheap checks pass (arithmetic on Num parameters, a field getter, a setter of a Num, a method that does arithmetic on fields) can run inline with none of that. The checks are the receiver's class for an instance member and the Num-ness of what the body takes as Num. A failed check takes the full path, which is safe because nothing has been written before any check.","files":null}]}